    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0388" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <head>199. Telegram From the Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commander in Chief,
                    European Command (Lemnitzer)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d199-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-06-08T01:10:00+00:00">June 8, 1967,
                    0110Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>7347. Subj: USS <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> (U).</p>
                <p>Refs: a. JCS 7337/072230Z Jun 67;<anchor n="2" xml:id="d199-f2"/> b. COMSIXTHFLT
                    071503Z Jun 67 (Notal).<anchor n="3" xml:id="d199-f3"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>(U) Cancel ref a.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>(TS) Reg <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> comply new op areas defined
                        last sentence para 2 ref b, until further notice, i.e., not closer than 100
                        NM to Israel, Syria, Egypt and 25 NM to Cyprus.<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d199-f4"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d199-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d199-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, NSC Histories, Middle East
                    Crisis, Vol. 7, Appendix H. Top Secret; Immediate. Repeated Immediate to CNO,
                    CINCLANT, CINCLANTFLT, CINCUSNAVEUR, COMSIXTHFLT, CTF 64, USS LIBERTY,
                    HQ-NSAEUR, NSAEUR OFF GERMANY, DIRNSA, DIRNAVSECGRU, ADIRNAVSECGRU,
                    DIRNAVSECGRULANT, DIRNAVSECGRUEUR.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f2" n="2" xml:id="d199-f2-content">
                <p> JCS telegram 7337 to USCINCEUR, 072230Z Jun 67, modified the instructions in JCS
                    6724 (<ref target="#d118">Document 118</ref>) to provide that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> should approach no closer than 20 NM to the
                    UAR and 15 NM to Israel. (Johnson Library, National Security File, NSC
                    Histories, Middle East Crisis, Vol. 7, Appendix H)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f3" n="3" xml:id="d199-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d192">Document 192</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f4" n="4" xml:id="d199-f4-content">
                <p>The U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> did not receive this message. See
                        <ref target="#d217">Document 217</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
